From edd6dc6b2c3ce82f64d567930edad27fbfc77255 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bradley Gleave <bradley@bradleytgpcoaching.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:04:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(importer): expand the native provenance ledger and type
 the reconstruction target
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

S8-B of the native contract (docs/decisions/2026-09-24-s8-native-contract.md,
§3.3 with the A2 closure): migration 20270122000000_scout_native_provenance_expand
creates ImportNativeProvenance, one row per (coach_id, source_namespace,
entity_type, source_id) recording which native TGP object a canonical source
entity became (native_kind, native_id) or why it did not (outcome unresolved,
native_id NULL, reason required). Closed CHECKs on native_kind and outcome, a
composite RESTRICT foreign key to ImportIntent, RLS forced with service_role the
only writer, and anon/authenticated denied by privilege and by policy.
ScoutReconstructionLedger gains a nullable target_kind, closed by CHECK and
requiring a target_id; the N/Q1/C writer never names it and keeps working
unchanged on the expanded schema.

down.sql refuses once any provenance row or typed ledger row exists (forward
repair only) and otherwise removes exactly what this migration added.

Schema-only: no writer code. The disposable PG 17 proof (test/rls-g2-s8b.spec.ts
with its g2-s8b-* helpers, lane s8-b, port 55511) covers expand exactness, rerun
refusal, mixed-version OLD/candidate writers, constraint and role refusals, and
the refusing down; it runs only under its own explicit fixture and is excluded
from the default Jest project.
